<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Backup rules (API < 31). ALLOWLIST, NOT DENYLIST.

   This file used to name the handful of stores that must NOT be copied. That is the wrong
   shape for the problem: the failure is never "somebody wrote the wrong rule", it is
   "somebody added a store and did not think about this file", which is invisible in the diff
   that adds the store. The app grew a dozen stores that way — including voiid_recovery, which
   holds the master secret for the encrypted account backup — and every one of them was being
   copied to Google's cloud.

   So the list is inverted. Only what is named here leaves the device, and anything added
   tomorrow is excluded by construction. BackupRulesTest enforces both halves: it fails the
   build if this file grows an <exclude>, if it names anything outside the portable set, or if
   a preference store appears in the source that nobody has classified.

   WHAT IS PORTABLE, and why only this: cosmetic per-install settings that identify nobody,
   carry no message, and are not wrapped by a Keystore key that cannot travel with them.

   WHAT IS NOT, and why it can never be:
     * Every EncryptedSharedPreferences store. The Keystore master key never leaves the
       device, so a restored copy is undecryptable ciphertext that crashes the app on launch
       (see SecurePrefs) — and a leak if it ever were decryptable.
     * files/messages/ (message shards), files/media/ (decrypted media), voiid_messages.json
       and its .tmp — plaintext belonging to this device's identity generation.
     * databases/voiid.db — the local Room cache of chats, calls and address-book names.
     * The address book, consent records and privacy choices, which are personal data
       regardless of encryption.

   The user-authorised account backup is a SEPARATE, deliberate path (RecoveryStore +
   BackupService): end-to-end encrypted under a secret the user holds, restored by an explicit
   action after sign-in. Nothing here is a substitute for it, and it is unaffected by this file.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="voiid_appearance.xml"/>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="voiid_prefs.xml"/>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="voiid_game_settings.xml"/>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="voiid_game_audio.xml"/>
</full-backup-content>
